From: VintagePomelo maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: honor the image's large-address-aware flag by default

Proton forces large-address-aware operation when WINE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE
is unset. This changes the address-space contract for every non-LAA PE32
image, including legacy games whose pointer arithmetic assumes addresses
below 2 GiB. An executable-name exception cannot cover renamed launchers
or games started by another Windows process.

Default to the PE header's IMAGE_FILE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE flag. Keep the
existing WINE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE=1 override for callers that explicitly
request the larger address space. An override of 0 still honors an image
that declares LAA; it does not strip the image's flag.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -5508,4 +5508,7 @@ static int need_override_large_address_aware(void)
-        needs_override = !str /* on by default */ || atoi(str) == 1;
+        /* Honor the PE address-space contract unless the caller explicitly
+         * opts into the larger address space. This also covers renamed
+         * launchers and children created by Windows applications. */
+        needs_override = str && atoi(str) == 1;
     }
     return needs_override;
 }
